<figcaption>Precision is TP / (TP + FP): when it answers, is it right? Recall is TP / (TP + FN): of the real values, how many did it find?</figcaption></figure>
<p>True negatives appear in neither formula on purpose. If a clause is missing from 80% of contracts, a model that always says “not present” scores 80% accuracy and zero recall. Accuracy would make it look good; recall tells the truth.</p>
